WEBVTT

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:03.900
[Soft electronic music begins.]

00:01:22.400 --> 00:01:25.592
Behind these flags, a siren is moving.

00:01:25.932 --> 00:01:27.804
Can you tell which way it went?

00:01:28.140 --> 00:01:32.676
Outside the cabinet, a cart carries a siren along a rail.

00:01:33.015 --> 00:01:35.535
A fixed horn receives its tone.

00:01:35.535 --> 00:01:38.391
The source stays at 100 Hz.

00:01:38.723 --> 00:01:41.771
Watch the wavefronts ahead of an approaching source.

00:01:42.098 --> 00:01:44.118
They arrive closer together.

00:01:44.118 --> 00:01:47.426
As the source recedes, they spread apart.

00:01:47.765 --> 00:01:52.541
Inside, nine tuned rods turn the shift into visible motion.

00:01:52.890 --> 00:01:55.940
Shorter rods respond to higher frequencies.

00:01:55.940 --> 00:01:58.722
Longer rods respond to lower ones.

00:01:59.057 --> 00:02:02.513
Compare the first and last events in the same run.

00:02:02.848 --> 00:02:05.568
The cart first approaches the horn quickly.

00:02:05.568 --> 00:02:08.752
In the last event, it quickly recedes.

00:02:09.098 --> 00:02:13.850
The model sees one interior image
per event, plus the initial frame.

00:02:14.182 --> 00:02:17.926
Its task is to recover all six cart settings in order.

00:02:18.265 --> 00:02:22.897
Across 20 apparatuses, CaveBench asks the same question.

00:02:23.223 --> 00:02:25.167
What happened outside the view?
